# Scripts

All scripts live in `scripts/` at the repo root. Run them from anywhere; each resolves paths relative to the repo root.

## `scripts/check-deps.sh`

Checks shared and project-specific tools using `projects.json`.

- Accepts a project ID or `all` (default), plus optional `--env production|wokwi`
- Required globally: `python3` and PlatformIO CLI (`pio`)
- Checks Wokwi only when the selected scope includes it
- Optional: PlatformIO IDE extension (CLI is enough to build)
- Exits non-zero if a required tool is missing

Run this first when setting up a new machine: `./scripts/check-deps.sh`

## `scripts/build.sh`

Builds registered firmware projects with PlatformIO.

- Usage: `./scripts/build.sh <project|all> [--env production|wokwi] [--target upload]`
- Runs project pre-build hooks from `projects.json`
- `scripts/build-firmware.sh` is a temporary `justin` migration wrapper for documented `-e`, `-t`, and `-v` usage only

Use this instead of calling `pio` directly.

## `scripts/stage.sh`

Stages a verified production package under `dist/<project>/<version>/`.

- Usage: `./scripts/stage.sh <project|all>`
- Copies bootloader, partitions, and a stable `firmware.bin`
- Writes `metadata.json` with project, version, environment, chip, offsets, and hashes
- Production builds also stage automatically after a successful compile

## `scripts/publish.sh`

Publishes browser-installer binaries for a registered project after a successful production build.

- Usage: `./scripts/publish.sh <project|all>`
- Restages from the production build, then copies only after package metadata matches the registry
- Rejects cross-project, version, chip, environment, offset, and hash mismatches
- Requires a prior build; exits with an error if any file is missing
- `scripts/update-web-installer.sh` is a temporary compatibility wrapper for `justin`

## `scripts/bump-version.sh`

Increments one registered project's version file.

- Usage: `./scripts/bump-version.sh <project> [--major|--minor|--patch]`
- Defaults to a patch bump when no flag is provided
- Uses strict `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` semver

Typical release workflow:

```bash
./scripts/bump-version.sh justin
./scripts/build.sh justin
./scripts/publish.sh justin
```

`./scripts/deploy <project> --patch|--minor|--major` does that sequence, then
creates one scoped commit and a `<project>/v<version>` tag. It restores the
version file and skips the commit if a step fails. Add `--push` only when the
user has asked to publish the tag. See `migration/stage-9-release-policy.md`.

The [browser installer](https://justinmahar.github.io/esp32-tinker/) (esp-web-tools) serves these files from GitHub Pages. OTA updates on a flashed device use the app partition binary only; the browser installer flashes the full image.

## `scripts/build-site.sh` / `scripts/preview-site.sh`

Build or preview the Astro catalog in `site/`.

- Requires Node.js and npm
- Preview URL: `http://localhost:4321/esp32-tinker/`
- `scripts/preview-installer.sh` is a compatibility wrapper around `preview-site.sh`

## `scripts/validate.sh` / `scripts/validate-site.sh` / `scripts/ci-matrix.sh`

CI helpers used by `.github/workflows/`.

- `validate.sh` loads `projects.json` and runs `scripts/tests`
- `ci-matrix.sh` prints the buildable project × environment matrix
- `validate-site.sh` checks published `firmware.bin` packages against the registry and a built `site/dist`
- Firmware CI and Pages deploy stay in separate workflows

## New firmware from starter

When copying `firmware/starter-template`, add Wokwi in the same change as the
hardware profile. A buildable project needs `[env:wokwi]` (`WOKWI_SIM=1`),
`wokwi.toml`, a `diagram.json` whose wires match `hardware/<profile>.h`, and
`"wokwi": "wokwi"` in `projects.json`. Use `starter-max7219` (MAX7219) or
`starter-hub75` (HUB75) as the simulator reference. See
`firmware/starter-template/README.md`.

## Deploy / Dev

If the user names a project to prepare for deploy:
- Run `./scripts/build.sh <project>`

If they say go back to development mode for a named project:
- Run `./scripts/build.sh <project> --env wokwi`

If they do not name a project, ask which one.